==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croconator]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*10 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Super Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Dober]] spawns as the boss after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Reach [[Worker Cat]] Lv.4, then slowly start to expand your army. Good meatshield choices could be both [[Eraser Cat]] and [[Manic Eraser Cat]], who will keep Dark Dober in place well enough, or just [[Kinjirou Cat]] can also do the job. As for unique options to put [[Metal Enemies]] on spot, there's [[Li'l Mohawk Cat]] and/or [[Future Cat]].

Though [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dark Lazer]] is the main unit that you will use to deal with Dark Dober, you shouldn't spam her so often - manage your resources well until you are done with Super Metal Hippoe and Sir Metal Seal, after which you are free to spam her.

Some good [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] that can endure Dark Dober's destruction for a bit include [[Catasaurus]], [[Cat Researcher]], [[Curry Cat]] and [[Soba Cat]]. [[Octopus Cat]] can be very useful, as even if it doesn't stay on the battlefield for too long, it can protect your Critters from Dark Dober's [[Mini-Wave]]s.

